        "timestamp": 1780393222,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 'Crazy': Trump-Netanyahu tensions flare over Iran and Hezbollah Issued on: 02/06/2026 - 11:40 US President Donald Trump said on Monday that Israel and Hezbollah had agreed to stop fighting, adding that Iran talks were moving rapidly after seeming to falter over Israel's Lebanon offensive. But there were fresh signs of tensions between the United States and Israel. Netanyahu appeared to cast doubt on any truce with Hezbollah – while a report in the US news outlet Axios said that Trump called the Israeli premier \"crazy\" and accused him of putting Iran peace talks at risk. For more, FRANCE 24’s Stuart Norval is joined by our International Affairs commentator Philip Turle, and Noga Tarnopolsky reporting from Jerusalem. 02/06/2026 Trump says Iran talks moving fast despite threat to widen war 02/06/2026 Russian attack on Ukraine kills at least 14 and traps others in damaged buildings 02/06/2026 Europe Pancreatic cancer: Dr. Pudlarz praises 'new generation targeted therapy' that inhibits gene mutation 02/06/2026 Health 'Healthy consensus in Israel' on pursuing Lebanon campaign, expert says 01/06/2026 Middle East Pro-Trump candidate lead in Colombia 'part of Donroe doctrine' asserting itself in region 01/06/2026 Americas Trump says Israel and Hezbollah have agreed to dial back fighting 01/06/2026 'Not Western version of democracy': 147 constituencies allegedly excluded from Ethiopia's election 01/06/2026 Africa Beaufort Castle: Israel hoists flag over castle in southern Lebanon 01/06/2026 Lebanon"
